      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This prospective, multicenter, observational study was designed to assess the in-hospital prognostic importance of renal insufficiency among patients presenting with acute coronary syndrome (ACS). One third of patients with ACS presented with renal insufficiency. After adjustment for potential confounders, decreasing renal function was independently associated with in-hospital death, bleeding, and contrast-induced nephropathy."},
